Now I understand the task. Let me implement `apply_batch` per the spec:

- Empty input → `Ok(())`, no side effects
- Write every `(path, content)`, creating parent dirs as needed
- Backups in memory only (never extra files in target tree)
- On first write failure: restore previously-written files to prior content (delete if created by this call), then report `WriteFailed { path, message }`
- If rollback itself fails on some entries: report `RollbackIncomplete { restored, failed }`
- No stray files left behind
